-- title:
--   Cross-leg description of the geometric fibres of Theta_{f,ℓ}
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of a fake elliptic curve moduli problem with full level $n$ and an extra level $\ell$, over a complete unramified base. The data and hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), a positive integer $N$ which is squarefree (`hN`) and divisible by neither $r$ (`hrN`) nor $\bar r$ (`hrbarN`). A commutative domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`) such that $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ (`hunr`), together with a fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero. A commutative domain $Onr$ of characteristic zero over $\mathcal O$, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), $(\pi Onr)$ is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x) \equiv x^r \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Quaternionic data.** Rationals $a, b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and, at each finite place, is a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), with a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`) containing all rational integers (`hΛℤ`). Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ definite ($a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$) and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in it (`hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`), an adelic unit $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (`hn₁`) with `meetOrder R₁ n₁` Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$ (`hv`), the group $\Gamma_t$ of units which are integral for $R_1$ at every place other than $v$ (`hΓt`), elements $s_\ell$, $s_{f,\ell}$ indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ satisfying the four local and Hecke conditions `hs` (adelic components away from $r$ given by $s_\ell$, trivial at $r$, the diagonal $\ell$ times $s_{f,\ell}^{-1}$ lying in the level Hecke set or the prime Hecke set of `meetOrder R₁ n₁` according to whether $\ell \mid N$, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$), the subgroups $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`), and an element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`). Further orders $\Lambda_{1s}$ (maximal, with $\Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_{1s} = R_1$), $R_2 \leq R_1$ and $R_2' \leq \Lambda_{1s}$, each an order saturating the larger order after multiplication by a power of $r$, with $R_2 \leq R_2'$ and $R_2$, $R_2'$ stable under the main involution.
--
--   **Moduli schemes.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `pt` which is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳`). An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$ (`hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`), a fine moduli space $M$ with point map `ptF` (`hM`), a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ forming a level twist action (`hρ`), and a morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over the base, invariant under $\rho$ and compatible with the point maps (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴`) with the two degeneracy maps $d_0, d_1$ to $\mathcal X$ over the base, compatible with forgetting and with $\ell$-isogenies (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`), and Atkin–Lehner endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Reduction data and the uniformisation.** A coordinate map `coord` on $\Lambda$ with values in $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$-Witt pairs satisfying `hcoord` (additivity, unitality, Frobenius-twisted multiplicativity, injectivity, density and the trace condition); a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ along the unit section with `hA₀` asserting that $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$; endomorphism families $e, e'$ of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$ with degrees $r^{\deg\gamma}$, subject to the blocks `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (isogeny pairs preserving level, multiplicativity and scalars up to powers of $r$, faithfulness, the comparison of the induced action on the formal module with $\iota_0$ conjugated by a single matrix up to powers of $r$, labels in $\Lambda$ for the $n$-torsion, and the statement that over an algebraically closed field every $r$-power isogeny of a pullback of $A_0$ comes from $\Gamma_t$), and the blocks `hE5a`–`hE5g`, `hE6a`–`hE6f` for the actions $\hat e$ of $R_2$ and $\hat e'$ of $R_2'$ (additivity, commutation with $\Lambda$, preservation of level, unitality, multiplicativity, integers, the norm relation, compatibility with $e$, the joint formal comparison, injectivity and the $q$-divisibility criterion); these blocks are summarised here. A ring map $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2}\text{-Witt} \to Onr$, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $Onr/(r)$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $MD$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), a comparison $\eta$ from rigidified objects to $MD$ satisfying the three clauses of `hη` (injectivity up to isomorphism on admissible objects, naturality, and local representability), an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ with bounded denominators (`hE₀`), and the block `eD`, `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` identifying the functor of $MD$-points with the product of the functor of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps from $Onr$ and Deligne's functor $\Omega$ over $K_0$, naturally and bijectively, so that the first coordinate is the leg, the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-action corresponds to the $vdet$-twisted action, and $\pi$-translation corresponds to a Frobenius twist of the leg. Further: a map $\kappa$ from $Onr/(\pi)$ to $Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ transported by $\kappa$, of height $4 n_0$ (`hβ₀`), a full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$, the Atkin–Lehner block $A_{0w}$, $a_w$, $a_w'$, $b_w$, $b_w'$ with `hALw`, `hBSw`, `hBSwlev`, `hJOINTw`, the assignment $\Xi$ of $MD$-points to rigidified curves with `hΞleg`, `hΞnat`, `hΞiso`, `hΞdef`, a matrix $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with the translation compatibilities `heqΓ`, `heqW`, `heqS`, a group homomorphism $\theta_t : \Gamma_t \to G$, the uniformisation map $\Theta_f$ for $M$ with its block `hnat`, `hG`, `hi'`, `het`, `hfib`, `hC0e`, `hC0u`, `hC1e`, `hC1u`, `hC1p`, `hC2`, `hC2c`, `hC3`, `hC4`, `hC4pi`, `hC5`, the extra-level data $C_0(\ell)$, $A_{0s}(\ell)$ with `hLIs`, `hBSs`, `hBSslev`, `hJOINTs` and the stabiliser criterion `hSTAB` (an element $\gamma$ of $\Gamma_t$ preserves $C_0(\ell)$ if and only if $\gamma \in \Gamma_{t,\ell}$), the existence and uniqueness of transported extra level structures `hCLe`, `hCLu`, and the coarse level-$\ell$ families $\Theta_T$ with `hnatT`, `hVT`; these blocks are summarised here.
--
--   **Level $(n;\ell)$.** A prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ is fixed, together with a fine moduli space $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for curves with full level $n$ and extra level $\ell$ (`hMℓ`), the forgetful map $\pi_\ell : M_\ell \to M$ and the map $p_\ell : M_\ell \to \mathcal Y_\ell$ over the base, compatible with the point maps (`hπℓf`, `hπℓ`, `hpℓg`, `hpℓ`), and an action $\rho_\ell$ of $G$ on $M_\ell$ over the base, compatible with $\pi_\ell$, $p_\ell$ and with twisting of level structures (`hρℓf`, `hρℓπ`, `hρℓp`, `hρℓtw`). The level-$(n;\ell)$ uniformisation map $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ sends, for each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, a triple consisting of a leg $\psi : Onr \to B$, a Deligne datum $P$ over $B$ and an element of $G$ to a $B$-point of $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$; it is natural (`hnatℓ`), equivariant for $\rho_\ell$ in the $G$-variable (`hGℓ`), computes the level-$(n;\ell)$ moduli point attached to a rigidified curve with its normalised level data (`hVALℓ`), and is invariant under the twisted action of elements of $\Gamma_t$ lying in $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ combined with left translation by $\theta_t(\gamma)$ (`hiℓ`).
--
--   Two further hypotheses are assumed. First, `hfibℓ₁`, the one-leg fibre description: for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, every leg $\psi$, all Deligne data $P, P'$ over $k$ and all $g, g' \in G$, one has $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g) = \Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P'),g')$ if and only if there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_{t,\ell}$, $g' = \theta_t(\gamma)g$ and $(\psi,P')$ obtained from $(\psi,P)$ by the $vdet$-twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$. Second, `hblindℓ`, leg-blindness: over any Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, for legs $\psi, \psi'$, data $P, P'$, $g \in G$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_t \cap \Gamma_{t,\ell}$, if $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`, and if $\psi'(y) = \psi(Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0(\gamma))}y)$ for every $y \in Onr$ fixed by $Fr^{vdet(\iota_0(z))}$ for all $z \in \Gamma_t$ which are rational scalars with $\theta_t(z) = 1$, then $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi',P'),\theta_t(\gamma)g) = \Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent in $k$, for all $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\psi, \psi' : Onr \to k$, all Deligne data $P, P'$ over $k$ and all $g, g' \in G$:
--   $$\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g) = \Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi',P'),g')$$
--   if and only if there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ such that
--
--   (i) $\gamma \in \Gamma_{t,\ell}$, that is, $\gamma$ lies in $\Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$;
--
--   (ii) $g' = \theta_t(\gamma)\,g$;
--
--   (iii) $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$: for every full lattice $M$ over $\mathcal O$ in $K_0^2$, the line of $P'$ at $M$ is the preimage, under the base-changed action isomorphism, of the line of $P$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}\!\cdot\!M$;
--
--   (iv) for every $y \in Onr$ with the property that $Fr^{vdet(\iota_0(z))}y = y$ for every $z \in \Gamma_t$ which is a rational scalar multiple of $1$ and satisfies $\theta_t(z) = 1$, one has $\psi'(y) = \psi\bigl(Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0(\gamma))}y\bigr)$.
--
--   Thus the conclusion differs from `hfibℓ₁` in allowing two distinct legs $\psi, \psi'$: the twisted-action condition on the leg is replaced by the pullback condition (iii) on the Deligne datum together with the agreement (iv) of $\psi'$ with the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ on the elements of $Onr$ fixed by the relevant powers of $Fr$.
--
--   This is the two-leg (cross-leg) description of the geometric fibres of the level-$(n;\ell)$ Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation map $\Theta_{f,\ell}$: points of the rigid family coincide precisely up to the action of $\Gamma_t \cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ on the Drinfeld datum, the $G$-coordinate and the leg. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.fineFamilyT_fibre_of_translate_of_value_of_isAlgClosed_eq_oneLegC5`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.fineFamilyT_fibre_of_translate_of_value_of_isAlgClosed_eq_oneLegC5), where the one-leg description and leg-blindness are available on the same frame.
